  "evidence": "TEXT_C: Independence as the central goal (“trigger negotiations… followed by a… referendum”), creation of Scottish Defence Forces and removal of Trident with withdrawal from NATO, “zero tolerance” for community crime with a total handgun ban and a national vehicle register. TEXT_D: “Build a fair, free, open society,” pro‑EU and potential euro entry, equal age of consent and repeal of Section 28 with stronger anti‑discrimination laws, restorative justice and a Royal Commission on drugs, ambitious environmental targets with tax shifts to pollution and renewables.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_D consistently argues from GAL commitments—civil liberties, social liberalisation, supranationalism, environmentalism, and less‑authoritarian justice—while TEXT_C mixes GAL themes with TAN‑compatible emphases on national sovereignty/identity (independence, own forces) and order (“zero tolerance,” handgun ban). Given a TAN‑leaning electorate, TEXT_C is closer to those priorities than the predominantly GAL TEXT_D.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_C"
}
